\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {11}{\ignorespaces What the player and the server say to each other. The player says where it is, the server replies with where everyone is, and this repeats 20 times a second. Ping is how long it takes to hear back; a lost reply shows up as a missing number. The ENet backend does the same thing through Godot's own networking.\relax }}{7}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:flow}{{11}{7}{What the player and the server say to each other. The player says where it is, the server replies with where everyone is, and this repeats 20 times a second. Ping is how long it takes to hear back; a lost reply shows up as a missing number. The ENet backend does the same thing through Godot's own networking.\relax }{figure.caption.17}{}}
